Governor={{.governor_roll}} | paragraph={{.paragraph_roll}} | motion={{.motion_roll}} | detail={{.detail_roll}} | closure={{.closure_roll}}

{{if::{{.governor_roll}} <= 3}}
Governor — clean momentum:
Prioritize continuation, visible consequence, and concise movement over ornament.

{{elseif::{{.governor_roll}} <= 6}}
Governor — restraint and implication:
Build the largest emotion through behavior, refusal, selection of detail, silence, or contradiction before naming it.

{{elseif::{{.governor_roll}} <= 9}}
Governor — physical continuity:
Track bodies, objects, attention, exits, and obstacles. Emotional intensity cannot erase blocking.

{{elseif::{{.governor_roll}} <= 12}}
Governor — dialogue-pressure balance:
Let dialogue carry whichever function the scene actually gives it: pressure, information, routine, humor, affection, etiquette, explanation, or presence.
Do not force a tactical change merely because dialogue occurred.

{{elseif::{{.governor_roll}} <= 15}}
Governor — intimate compression:
Stay close to the active beat rather than expanding into broad history or summary.

{{elseif::{{.governor_roll}} <= 18}}
Governor — visual continuity:
Keep spatial and causal staging legible. Under Extended Pace this may support visible progression; under Close Pace it may simply make the current activity easy to inhabit.

{{else}}
Governor — lush but disciplined:
Rich prose is permitted when compatible with the selected Style. A paragraph may dwell, recur, describe, converse, or advance; no paragraph-level movement quota is created.
{{/if}}

{{if::{{.paragraph_roll}} <= 2}}
Paragraph governor:
Use a denser novel-like structure, but long paragraphs require internal movement.

{{elseif::{{.paragraph_roll}} <= 4}}
Paragraph governor:
Use shorter paragraphs and let white space create tension. Avoid monologue walls unless the scene requires one controlled speech.

{{elseif::{{.paragraph_roll}} <= 6}}
Paragraph governor:
Use staggered rhythm and distribute movement, thought, and sensory detail rather than front-loading description.

{{elseif::{{.paragraph_roll}} <= 8}}
Paragraph governor:
Use tight staccato paragraphs with distinct jobs: setup, pressure, turn, consequence, remainder.

{{elseif::{{.paragraph_roll}} <= 10}}
Paragraph governor:
Place one substantially heavier paragraph near the middle while keeping surrounding beats anchored in action and consequence.

{{else}}
Paragraph governor:
Vary length aggressively, including one brief paragraph and one layered fuller paragraph.
{{/if}}

{{if::{{.motion_roll}} <= 2}}
Motion:
Hold the scene in active suspension through withholding, obstruction, delay, or increased difficulty.

{{elseif::{{.motion_roll}} <= 4}}
Motion:
Let environment and spatial conditions materially alter action.

{{elseif::{{.motion_roll}} <= 6}}
Motion:
Use micro-movement—hands, breath, posture, objects, glances, or distance—to advance the beat.

{{elseif::{{.motion_roll}} <= 8}}
Motion:
Carry the previous action into a consequence rather than introducing an unrelated twist.

{{else}}
Motion:
Follow active Pacing. Under Extended Pace, a concrete choice, movement, completion, reveal, transition, or other scene-native change may carry the response onward. Under Close Pace, continued activity or deliberate stillness may be the whole response.
{{/if}}

{{if::{{.detail_roll}} <= 2}}
Detail:
Strip down. Retain details that earn their place through viewpoint, material texture, atmosphere, process, relation, humor, motif, clarity, or consequence.

{{elseif::{{.detail_roll}} <= 4}}
Detail:
Use one dominant anchor and let the response orbit it.

{{elseif::{{.detail_roll}} <= 6}}
Detail:
Keep detail sparse and let movement, dialogue, and silence carry more work.

{{elseif::{{.detail_roll}} <= 8}}
Detail:
Use moderate detail selected for character attention, danger, discomfort, desire, or power.

{{else}}
Detail:
Choose two or three strong details and return to one with changed meaning.
{{/if}}

{{if::{{.closure_roll}} <= 2}}
Ending:
Land cleanly but not safely. Preserve charge beneath the beat.

{{elseif::{{.closure_roll}} <= 4}}
Ending:
Withhold one motive, reaction, or implication.

{{elseif::{{.closure_roll}} <= 6}}
Ending:
End on consequence in body, room, relation, information, or silence.

{{else}}
Ending:
End on a turn that changes immediate pressure rather than fully resolving it.
{{/if}}
{{/if}}

